                <pb facs="0684" n="584" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg584"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/6358: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-02-13"><hi rendition="#italic">February 13,
                        1920</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received February 16—2:24 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>130. From Admiral McCully [,Sevastopol.]</p>
                <p>“16. February 13, 1 a.m. Agreement has been reached between Denikin and Supreme
                    Cossack Council but it is not whole hearted and effective. Terek agrees
                    unreservedly, Don with a ‘perplexed souland’, and Kuban with protest and mental
                    reservations. Conditions in Sevastopol point to repetition of Odessa events at
                    an early date.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
